  "question": {
    "text": "An octahedral complex of Co<sup>3</sup><sup>+</sup> is diamagnetic. The hybridisation involved in the formation of the complex is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "xqqeP",
      "text": "dsp<sup>2</sup>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DYVeV",
      "text": "d<sup>2</sup>sp<sup>3</sup>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "MTPXh",
      "text": "dsp<sup>3</sup>d",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4a1pe",
      "text": "sp<sup>3</sup>d<sup>2</sup>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math> <mrow> <msub> <mspace></mspace> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mn>7</mn> </mrow> </msub> <msup> <mtext>Co</mtext> <mrow> <mn>3</mn> <mo>+</mo> </mrow> </msup> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;has 24 Electrons i.e 6 electrons in inner 3d orbital of central metal ion for diamagnetic behaviour these d<sup>6</sup> Electrons have to be paired and due to pairing two inner d-orbitals get empty and hybridisation is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>.<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/EM0026103DUP01HIN.jpg\" style=\"width: 459px; height: 136px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
